# openOODA `ooda/std` — product standard library

Modules that **check + Backend-C build** on the pure path (`.oo` + thin C runtime).
No ambient FS or net. This tree is what product programs can import today.

Product-tracked set is 56 files: the historic 50 plus `fs/path.oo`, `text/regex_nfa.oo`,
`sec/objcap_hmac.oo`, `fs/stream.oo`, `encoding/base64.oo`, and `text/regex_dfa.oo`.
Other `.oo` files sitting in this directory are untracked Gemini drops, not product.
Org `../std` is not product. `std/prove_open80.oo` is the named org emit+gcc+run.

## Real (pure check + pure build)

| Module | Role | Caps |
|--------|------|------|
| `core/list.oo` | `list_is_empty` / `list_first` / `list_last` on `List[Int]` | none |
| `result.oo` | `Result[String,String]` helpers | none |
| `str.oo` | thin string wrappers | none |
| `math.oo` | IEEE-754 **double** wrappers. Float is not decimal. | none |
| `option.oo` | optional-string helpers as `Result` | none |
| `byte.oo` | `type Byte = Int` plus clamp/range. Check floor only. | none |
| `markup/{toml,yaml,xml}.oo` | path A one-line extract | none |
| `markup/json_schema.oo` | trivial `{}` id; `validate` always false | none |
| `archive/{tar,zip,gzip}.oo` | magic detect only. Not decompress. | none |
| `math/tensor.oo` | flat `List[Int]` tensor_new/get/set | none |
| `os/fs.oo` | read/write/exists/size | `&FsCap` family |
| `fs/stream.oo` | buffered fd read/write store | none |
| `encoding/base64.oo` | RFC 4648 encode/decode | none |
| `text/regex_nfa.oo` | `a+`, `a|b`, `[ab]` class scan | none |
| `text/regex_dfa.oo` | `dfa_compile` / `dfa_simulate` | none |
| `core/crypto.oo` | sha256, hmac, AES-128-ECB hex | none |
| `os/net.oo` | http/tcp/udp/tls + slot IO | `&NetCap` family |
| `os/process.oo` | spawn/wait/kill/exec | `&ProcessCap` |

**List:** `std/core/list.oo` is `List[Int]` only. Empty list returns `Err("empty")` for first/last.

**Process:** spawn / wait / kill are real (`fork` / `waitpid` / `kill`). Need ProcessCap (or old SysCap). Kill of pid 0 is refused. epoll / inotify / prctl stay residual Err under SysCap.

**Fixtures**

- Check: `oodac check std/result.oo` (and `str.oo`, `option.oo`, `byte.oo`, `core/list.oo`) — library OK without `main`.
- Build: `fixtures/std_list_main.oo`, `fixtures/std_result_main.oo`, `fixtures/std_str_main.oo` via `scripts/oodac_pure_build.oo`.
- Math: `fixtures/math_trig.oo` + `scripts/math_trig_smoke.oo`
- Markup / archive: `fixtures/std_markup_main.oo`, `fixtures/std_archive_main.oo`
- OPEN-76..79: `fixtures/open76_fd_stream.oo`, `open77_aes.oo`, `open78_base64.oo`, `open79_regex_dfa.oo`

## Residual

| Item | Honesty |
|------|---------|
| `os/gpu.oo` | GpuCap CPU/noop Ok. Device shaders Err. |
| Generic `List[T]` / nested lists | `core/list.oo` is `List[Int]` only |
| `Option[T]` sum types | Backend-C does not lower constructors. Use `option.oo`. |
| Generic `Result[T,E]` | runtime string payload only |
| Decimal float | product `Float` is IEEE-754 double |
| Full XML/YAML/TOML/JSON Schema | path A subsets only |
| tar/zip/gzip decompress | magic detect only |

Do **not** import an org sibling `std/src/ooda` tree from here. It is not this floor.

## Security

These modules must **not** open files, sockets, or env on their own.
Effectful `os/*` wrappers take a leading cap. Pure helpers wrap CHS string/list/result only.
